# SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000160  -  CAT II
# Debugging and trace information used to diagnose the web server must be
# disabled.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000160
group:           V-206413
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-001312
control_rev5:    SI-11

contribution:    Splunk Web exposes each debugging and trace facility the requirement names
                 as a distinct setting the product can turn off: the /debug REST endpoints
                 (enableWebDebug), the traceback rendered to the user
                 (request.show_tracebacks), the client-side JavaScript logger including the
                 mode that posts to a server endpoint (js_logger_mode), dashboard
                 performance metrics emitted to the browser console
                 (simple_xml_perf_debug), the development auto-restart facility
                 (engine.autoreload.on) and application server standard error reaching the
                 Splunk log (appServerProcessLogStderr).

governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] request.show_tracebacks equals false
check:           web.conf [settings] simple_xml_perf_debug not_equals true
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] appServerProcessLogStderr https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] enableWebDebug https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] engine.autoreload.on https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] js_logger_mode https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] request.show_tracebacks https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] simple_xml_perf_debug https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] enableWebDebug not_equals true
                 reason: "Whether or not the debug REST endpoints are accessible, for
                         example., /debug/**splat. Default: false"
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] js_logger_mode not_in Firebug|Server
                 reason: "js_logger_mode = [None | Firebug | Server]. The JavaScript Logger
                         mode. Available modes: None, Firebug, Server. Mode None: Does not
                         log anything. Mode Firebug: Use firebug by default if it exists, or
                         defer to the older less promiscuous version of firebug lite. Mode
                         Server: Log to a defined server endpoint... Default: None"
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] engine.autoreload.on not_equals true
                 reason: "Whether or not the appserver will auto-restart if it detects a
                         python file has changed. Default: false"
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] appServerProcessLogStderr not_equals true
                 reason: "If set to true, messages written to the standard error stream by
                         the Python-based application server processes will be logged to
                         splunkd.log under the 'UiAppServer' channel. This can be useful
                         when debugging issues when the appserver process fails to start.
                         However, some appserver code may print sensitive information such
                         as session ID strings to standard error so this defaults to
                         disabled. Default: false"
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Debugging and developer tooling shipped inside installed Splunk apps —
                 dashboard debug parameters, app-level logging and any diagnostic views an
                 app provides — is carried by the app developer and the app approval
                 process, not by web.conf.
external:        Interpreter-level tracing, core dumps and debug symbols on the host
                 running Splunk are carried by the operating system baseline.
external:        Where a reverse proxy or load balancer fronts Splunk, URI filtering of the
                 /debug path is an additional layer carried by that component and assessed
                 against its own baseline.

citation:        SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000160 check and fix text (CCI-001312, SI-11 a); no
                 product STIG rule shares CCI-001312. Splunk 10.x specification set
                 (Version 10.0.0): web.conf.spec:1295 enableWebDebug, default false,
                 controlling access to the debug REST endpoints; web.conf.spec:910
                 request.show_tracebacks, default true; web.conf.spec:379 js_logger_mode =
                 [None | Firebug | Server], default None; web.conf.spec:1054
                 simple_xml_perf_debug, default false; web.conf.spec:915
                 engine.autoreload.on, default false; web.conf.spec:1285
                 appServerProcessLogStderr, default false.
finding:         A debugging or trace facility remains enabled in web.conf [settings] —
                 enableWebDebug, simple_xml_perf_debug, engine.autoreload.on or
                 appServerProcessLogStderr is true, request.show_tracebacks is not false,
                 or js_logger_mode is set to Firebug or Server — so Splunk Web retains
                 diagnostic output the requirement directs be disabled; this is assessed at
                 the application layer alone, and developer tooling supplied inside
                 installed apps and host-level tracing are recorded as external
                 dependencies rather than as part of this finding.
